From a0590c556cdbf88373d38494a23f1503d39b0ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thorsten Blum <blum@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:11:02 +0200
Subject: hwrng: intel - return -ENOMEM when kmalloc_obj() fails
Git-commit: a0590c556cdbf88373d38494a23f1503d39b0ab2
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

intel_rng_mod_init() incorrectly returns -ENODEV when kmalloc_obj()
fails. Return -ENOMEM instead.

Fixes: ee527cd3a20c ("Use stop_machine_run in the Intel RNG driver")
Signed-off-by: Thorsten Blum <blum@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/char/hw_random/intel-rng.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/char/hw_random/intel-rng.c
+++ b/drivers/char/hw_random/intel-rng.c
@@ -349,6 +349,7 @@ static int __init intel_rng_mod_init(voi
 	intel_rng_hw = kmalloc(sizeof(*intel_rng_hw), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!intel_rng_hw) {
 		pci_dev_put(dev);
+		err = -ENOMEM;
 		goto out;
 	}
 
